<article class="env-lemma" id="0D4G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D4G">Lemma <span data-tag="0D4G">37.12.4</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of locally Noetherian schemes. Let $Z \subset S$ be a closed subscheme with $n$th infinitesimal neighbourhood $Z_ n \subset S$. Set $X_ n = Z_ n \times _ S X$. If $X_ n \to Z_ n$ is flat for all $n$, then $f$ is flat at every point of $f^{-1}(Z)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a translation of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0523" data-tag="0523">10.99.11</a> into the language of schemes. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>